# data is never committed - it is re-derivable from data/raw/manifest.jsonl
data/raw/*
data/interim/*
data/processed/*
data/external/*
!data/**/.gitkeep
!data/raw/manifest.jsonl

# routing artifacts (see docs/engineering/DATA_ENGINEERING.md sec 2)
*.osm.pbf
*.osrm*

# warehouse
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# run logs are never committed. they record every URL, SQL statement and
# shell command a run issued, so a single un-scrubbed line could publish a
# credential. re-derivable by re-running; not worth the risk.
logs/

# notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# os / editor
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# secrets
.env
*.key

# Coverage database. Binary, and it stores an ABSOLUTE path for every source
# file it measured -- 130 copies of the author's home directory. It was
# tracked until 2026-09-15.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Container/session scratch. Records internal hostnames and the paths of
# sandbox shared objects. Never useful, never publishable.
vnc_logs/

# manually-placed third-party data: re-obtainable via docs/data/ACQUISITION_GUIDE.md
data/external/*
!data/external/README.md
!data/external/**/TEMPLATE.csv

# ...with three exceptions, because "re-obtainable" is not true of all of it.
# The Zillow tables (130MB) are one download and stay out. These are not:
#
#   facilities.csv / national_facilities.csv  are the TARGET VARIABLE. They
#     were assembled by hand across several sessions of classification
#     batches against OSHA records, press releases and permit filings. No
#     URL returns them. Losing them loses the project. 22KB combined.
#   nlrb_cases_amazon.csv  is a filtered export from an interactive search
#     that caps results and has no stable query URL; reproducing it means
#     redoing the search under six spellings of the company name. 877KB.
#
# Small, irreplaceable, and the whole reason the repo exists.
#
# NOTE ON THE PATTERN BELOW. `data/external/*` above excludes the SUBDIRECTORY
# itself, and git will not descend into an excluded directory, so a bare
# `!data/external/facility_panel/facilities.csv` silently never matches. The
# directory has to be re-admitted first, then its contents re-excluded, then
# the wanted files admitted. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
!data/external/facility_panel/
data/external/facility_panel/*
!data/external/facility_panel/facilities.csv
!data/external/facility_panel/national_facilities.csv

!data/external/nlrb/
data/external/nlrb/*
!data/external/nlrb/nlrb_cases_amazon.csv
!data/external/nlrb/HOWTO.md

# CBP ZIP x industry detail: 7 vintages, ~120MB, one curl each. Regenerable
# from https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/cbp/datasets/{year}/zbp{yy}detail.zip
data/raw/cbp_zip_detail/

# TIGER ZCTA boundaries (504MB) and cached Overpass responses: regenerable.
data/raw/tiger_zcta/
data/raw/osm_landuse/

# Satellite dating output. NOT reproducible from this repo -- it came from a
# Colab run against Microsoft Planetary Computer, whose imagery host the
# university proxy blocks. Tracked because it is the EVIDENCE for a
# documented negative result (docs/data/SATELLITE.md) and cannot be
# regenerated here.
!data/external/satellite/
!data/external/satellite/*.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MWPVL 2025 Q1 network article, and the two artefacts derived from it.
#
# TRACKED BECAUSE THEY CANNOT BE RE-FETCHED. The publisher states in the
# article itself that they are withdrawing it from free circulation ("in
# future we will no longer be updating this information online"), so the
# saved copy IS the source. An audit on 2026-09-14 found the file previously
# archived here was a DIFFERENT, smaller document -- 871 KB, whose image 34 is
# a 14x16 thumbnail where the real one is the 828x26480 table strip that was
# actually OCR'd. The extraction was therefore not reproducible from this
# repository at all. Both files are kept: the 2012 vintage for comparison,
# and the 2025 Q1 article that the panel is built from.
#
# The two CSVs are derived and regenerable ONLY while the PDF survives, which
# is exactly the condition that is ending.
!data/raw/mwpvl/
!data/raw/mwpvl/*.pdf
# ...but NOT the OCR intermediates underneath it. Un-ignoring the directory
# re-included these; they are ~20 MB of extracted page images and word-
# coordinate TSVs, both rebuilt in minutes by scripts/grid/run_ocr.sh from
# the PDF above.
data/raw/mwpvl/images/
data/raw/mwpvl/tsv/
!data/interim/mwpvl_facilities.csv
!data/external/facility_panel/national_facilities_expanded.csv
# Census Batch Geocoder output for those 700 rows. Re-runnable in seconds IF
# the endpoint stays up and free, which is exactly the assumption that failed
# for the MWPVL source. 455 matched coordinates cost nothing to keep.
!data/external/facility_panel/geocoded_expanded.csv

# Good Jobs First Subsidy Tracker, Amazon parent, downloaded 2026-09-14.
# PAID (USD 25) and NOT re-fetchable from this host, which gets HTTP 403 from
# the endpoint. 349 KB. Tracked for the same reason as the MWPVL article: a
# source that cannot be re-downloaded is evidence, not a cache.
!data/external/subsidies/
!data/external/subsidies/*.csv

# Relocated system binaries for the grid OCR run: tesseract, glibc and the
# dynamic loader, ~20 MB. Built by scripts/grid/bundle_tesseract.sh, valid
# only for one OS/arch, and rebuildable in seconds on any host that has
# tesseract. Never in git.
vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC REPOSITORY OVERRIDE (2026-09-15)
#
# Everything above was written while this repository was private, where the
# governing concern was preserving sources that cannot be re-downloaded.
# Publishing inverts that reasoning for two of them: a file we cannot re-fetch
# is still a file we have no right to redistribute. Both were verified as
# COMMITTABLE by `git check-ignore -q` before these rules were added. They sit
# last in the file so they win.

# Good Jobs First Subsidy Tracker, Amazon parent. Purchased under a USD 25
# subscription licence; redistribution is not ours to grant. The derived
# aggregates ship instead, in outputs/metrics/subsidies.json, and
# docs/DATA_SOURCES.md says where to buy the original.
data/external/subsidies/

# MWPVL International industry reports: third-party copyright, and the
# publisher states in the article that it is being withdrawn from free
# circulation. The FACTS extracted from them do ship, attributed, as
# data/interim/mwpvl_facilities.csv -- facts are not copyrightable, the
# document is.
data/raw/mwpvl/*.pdf

# THE TWO FILES THAT MAKE THIS REPOSITORY REPRODUCIBLE WITHOUT A DOWNLOAD.
#
# `data/raw/*` and `data/processed/*` above exclude everything on the grounds
# that it is re-derivable. True, but re-deriving these two means ~4 GB of
# downloads, three API keys and the better part of a working day -- so in
# practice the exclusion made the repository un-runnable for anyone who
# cloned it. With these two present, `make cost model scope figures`
# reproduces the cost model, the choice model, the covariate search, the
# leakage tests and every figure with NO network access and NO keys.
#
# 16.4 MB against GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. The cheapest thing this
# project can do to be useful to a stranger.
!data/processed/panel.parquet
!data/interim/cbp_detail.parquet

# THE DIRECTORY READMEs UNDER data/.
#
# Everything under data/ is excluded by file above, which caught the READMEs
# too -- so the directories that most need to explain themselves to someone
# who cloned the repo (they arrive nearly empty, on purpose) were the ones
# that shipped no explanation at all. Each has to be re-admitted by name:
# a `data/**/README.md` glob does not reach into a directory git has already
# excluded outright. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
!data/raw/README.md
!data/interim/README.md
!data/processed/README.md
!data/external/facility_panel/README.md
!data/external/nlrb/README.md
